^["stream"]{
 >>[2026-07-20] observe — repo pins typescript ~5.9.3; TS 6 (bridge) and TS 7 (native Go) are both released. TS 7 has no stable programmatic API until ~7.1.
 >>[2026-07-20] observe — tsconfig.base.json still sets baseUrl (deprecated in 6, hard error in 7). types not explicit (6/7 default types to []).
 >>[2026-07-20] observe — extensions/vscode-spw pins typescript ^5.2.0 while root uses ~5.9.3 — pin drift.
 >>[2026-07-20] observe — package uses @typescript-eslint/parser ^8.57.2; dual-install will be required if default tsc becomes 7 before eslint supports native API.
 >>[2026-07-20] decide — ladder order is non-skippable: prep on 5.9 → 6 clean → dual 7+6 API → optional default flip. Speed claims require perf-audit baselines.
 >>[2026-07-20] decide — never land ignoreDeprecations:6.0 on mainline; treat deprecations as rung A/B work.
 >>[2026-07-20] taste — version story should be as clear as Spw sigils: one command, one compiler, one documented fallback.
 >>[2026-10-12 14:38] observe — rung A probe on 5.9.3: a scratch copy of tsconfig.base.json with baseUrl removed and its paths made absolute, same include set as tsconfig.typecheck.json, type-checks with exit 0 and no errors (7 s). The paths entries are ./-prefixed and a grep for bare imports from src, packages, scripts, lib, or docs finds none, so root baseUrl is not load-bearing. extensions/vscode-spw/tsconfig.json is a second baseUrl site ('../..') whose paths are written relative to it without ./, so removing it there needs the paths rewritten; that site was not tested and ~[2] did not name it.
 >>[2026-10-12 14:38] observe — eslint ^9.39.4 and @typescript-eslint/parser ^8.57.2 are devDependencies, but the repo has no eslint config file and no package script invokes eslint; npm run lint is lint:spw plus lint:docs. Every vitest config sets globals false and every describe-using test file checked imports from vitest; @types/node is the root types package and @types/vscode belongs to the extension.
 >>[2026-10-12 14:38] revise — ~[1] landed in a333db8d and moved to ^[done]. ~[2] split into ~[2] (baseUrl), ~[10] (explicit types), ~[11] (extension pin and its own baseUrl); ~[9] drops the non-standard sigil suffix. ?[types_array] resolved and moved to ^[done]. ?[eslint_peer] rewritten as ?[eslint_gate] because eslint may not be a gate at all, which changes the case for the rung C dual-install. Card next corrected for the second baseUrl site.
 >>[2026-10-12 15:00] revise — corrected ?[eslint_gate]: eslint.config.js exists at the repo root, so the gap is that no package.json script runs eslint, not a missing config; routed from lukewarm-backlog ?[eslint_unwired].
}

^["open"]{
